## 6. Jackpot Testing — Test Design

| ID | Test Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC-031 | Verify jackpot eligibility rules | Only eligible bets or players qualify |
| TC-032 | Trigger a jackpot-winning event in a test environment | The event is processed according to the jackpot rules |
| TC-033 | Verify jackpot award and wallet update | Award and balance changes are consistent |
| TC-034 | Submit the same jackpot event twice | The jackpot award is not duplicated |
| TC-035 | Simulate an interruption during jackpot processing | Recovery does not result in a duplicate award or inconsistent state |

**Note:** Jackpot scenarios are test designs. They require a jackpot implementation or a suitable test simulator before execution.

## Test Execution Notes

- Record actual results and execution status when each test is run.
- Attach evidence such as Postman responses, SQL query results, and application logs.
- Verify expected behavior against the API specification and business rules.
- Do not include production credentials, secrets, or real customer data.
